    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 327,
        "text": "Welcome to the Riverside Community Transport Forum. I'm Maya Chen, and today we're evaluating three policy claims about our local bus network. First, let me introduce our speakers: Daniel Ortiz from the city planning office, and Priya Nair, who chairs the residents' committee. Daniel, can you start with the first claim?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "c1da308d49742bae0e9afda7aa93286d796dba8f0bc22df844c46bd3f59513b1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 337,
        "sourceEnd": 687,
        "text": "Thanks, Maya. Claim one says the new bus lane on Mill Street reduced average journey times by fifteen minutes. That's not accurate. Our data shows the reduction was about five minutes during peak hours, not fifteen. The fifteen-minute figure came from a single test run on a Sunday morning with almost no traffic. So the claim overstates the benefit.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "dd852bf6c045e1cea459e04370e258d1962b6a6f66164c662f604a20b8413c19",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 696,
        "sourceEnd": 1016,
        "text": "I'd like to add something there. Residents have told us the bus lane helps, but the improvement is modest. Several people said their morning commute is now about eight minutes shorter, which is good, but not fifteen. Also, the bus lane is only on the northbound side, so southbound buses still get stuck near the market.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "bce16871247ec28bc48b2b4ed32b503fc25829b1114af4cbcc8b29c3a96f5504",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1024,
        "sourceEnd": 1141,
        "text": "Good point. Let's move to claim two. It says the new ticket machines at Central Station accept cash. Is that correct?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "b86fd399c039f57a686c219df48d10331eb06004e8464d518b3b5ee63048fe63",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1151,
        "sourceEnd": 1419,
        "text": "Partly. The machines accept coins, but not paper notes. So if you only have a ten-pound note, you can't use the machine. You have to go to the ticket counter, which closes at six in the evening. After six, passengers with only notes cannot buy a ticket at the station.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "64f27e7e660afef3db396325cf3d4e4a465d800ba2dfc427b7eb2154dc1e8f2d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 1428,
        "sourceEnd": 1594,
        "text": "And that's a real problem for older residents. Many of them prefer cash. The committee has asked the council to add note acceptance, but there's no date for that yet.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "3f2ca1ed0d1460c3ae6db4c0f3c6dfc0d5d4b020c7d8bc3c58c7893ec67b54c6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1602,
        "sourceEnd": 1704,
        "text": "Thank you. Now claim three: the weekend bus service to the hospital runs every twenty minutes. Daniel?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "b258a4ed6278d88408c00ce18c3f2c120a827bba862bdd539fb98f3bfec8e898",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1714,
        "sourceEnd": 1943,
        "text": "That claim is false. On Saturdays, the bus runs every thirty minutes. On Sundays, it runs every forty minutes. The twenty-minute frequency applies only on weekdays. So the weekend service is less frequent than the claim suggests.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "e90afd004ef82e840511bd82b9056e7bcf535a555d7a5cc01cf49f3a9a3a9074",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 1952,
        "sourceEnd": 2115,
        "text": "I checked the timetable myself last Saturday. I waited thirty-five minutes because one bus was cancelled. So even the thirty-minute schedule isn't always reliable.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "48a2f2a1501a4e589f264c1743afa07dccac1769551dd94716f1241ccc5b237b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2123,
        "sourceEnd": 2198,
        "text": "Let's compare the three claims. Which one is most misleading, in your view?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "a0f1feeaf067b3e5f6ffaaf52bee55b9c8e8380889a47716bbaa6b3dc060c4ba",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2208,
        "sourceEnd": 2383,
        "text": "I'd say claim one, because it uses a number from an unusual test run and presents it as typical. Claim two is partly true, and claim three is simply wrong about the frequency.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "d1e4e5c88af5c44996472a6ac445e68511b2d1732f19b449e1163b992640ee32",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 2392,
        "sourceEnd": 2570,
        "text": "I agree that claim one is the most misleading. But I'd add that claim two has the biggest daily impact on vulnerable passengers. So the claims differ in both accuracy and impact.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "14f0c294c9cbbf3df23d99903a581e0e7128d3d3eba5a49d866c5592eabd9ce1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2578,
        "sourceEnd": 2671,
        "text": "That's a useful distinction. Before we finish, can you summarize the changes since last year?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "a7ceb76c8667d06fa575f78d1bfc9f6f2775d770395a876640299b7c87d460da",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2681,
        "sourceEnd": 2937,
        "text": "Yes. Since last year, the number of bus lanes has increased from two to three. Average journey times have fallen slightly, by about three minutes overall. And the number of ticket machines has grown from four to seven, though most still don't accept notes.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "3f2a2cd5ea7f56d061d5f65e7277221c75da0fbec88e7de3c7d37428689dcdc6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 2946,
        "sourceEnd": 3108,
        "text": "Also, the residents' committee has grown from twelve members to twenty. We now meet once a month instead of every two months. So public involvement is increasing.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "50ed808994db29a52337e3f74633abf8b8bccb850a4a28775df7bc5da449fc47",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3116,
        "sourceEnd": 3310,
        "text": "Thank you both. To conclude: claim one overstates a benefit, claim two is only partly correct, and claim three is false for weekends. We'll publish these findings on the forum website next week.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "e25463f84aa766ce087cbb4cd4f0c88927a673c7b43e0b0a81ef34b00731baf7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
